Print the resolved geometry: shapes, anchors, lines, labels and the placement graph

Usage: kashika inspect [OPTIONS] <FILE> [IDS]...

Arguments:
  <FILE>    Input .kash file, or `-` for stdin
  [IDS]...  Only show these ids

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>          [default: text] [possible values: text, json]
      --stdin-name <STDIN_NAME>  File name to report for stdin input
      --allow-path               Allow file references outside the input file's directory
      --include <FILE>           Allow this one file outside the input file's directory (repeatable; relative to the current directory)
      --ports                    List the endpoints on each shape side and the lines that use them
      --corridors <X1,Y1,X2,Y2>  Free horizontal and vertical intervals inside the rectangle x1,y1,x2,y2; without ids, prints only these
  -h, --help                     Print help
